/-!
# FHE.Float.RNELow — the low-limb decryption transcription against recorded library outputs   (UNTRUSTED)

The `#guard`s run the TRUSTED transcription `Spec.DecryptBFVLow.decLow1` with the
round-to-nearest-even arithmetic `FHE.Float.RNE.rneA` (uncontracted: the libraries used contain
no FMA instruction) on residue vectors given to the real OpenFHE v1.6.1 `PKEBFVRNS::Decrypt` as the
phase of a ciphertext with fewer limbs than `Q`, and check the library's returned coefficient bit
for bit. The values are recorded outputs of the library's routine, which the transcription
reproduces bit for bit. The first rows are at `t = 18014398510661633 ≈ 2⁵⁴` with four 60-bit
limbs; `decLowOK?` refuses these parameters at every level and noise bound
(`Challenge.BFVDecryptLow`). The BEHZ rows at the end are recorded outputs of the integer
routine at the full level.
-/

